Provenance & Attribution Summary:
1. All Python modules (`mini_verl/*.py`, `mini_verl/examples/*.py`, `mini_verl/tests/*.py`) were
   written from scratch in pure CPU PyTorch (~2,000 lines) for pedagogical clarity and deterministic
   laptop execution. No source files were copied verbatim from upstream verl, vLLM, SGLang, PyTorch
   FSDP, Megatron-LM, or Ray.
2. Public API identifiers — class names (`DataProto`, `WorkerGroup`, `RayPPOTrainer`,
   `ActorRolloutRefWorker`), decorator names (`@register`, `Dispatch.*`), algorithm formulas,
   configuration key paths, and metric names (`actor/pg_loss`, `timing_s/*`) — intentionally mirror
   the verl project at tag `v0.9.1` (commit `1876b06d0a3e4e71e06230be10af14492ca8a75b`,
   https://github.com/verl-project/verl, Copyright 2024 Bytedance Ltd. and/or its affiliates and the
   verl contributors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0) so readers can study the toy
   implementation side by side with the production codebase.
3. Short configuration snippets and CLI invocation examples quoted in the companion book follow
   verl v0.9.1 documentation and example scripts under Apache License 2.0 attribution.

